    "overview": "A short climbing trip from the Annapurna Circuit, to a symmetrical snow pyramid above the village of Pisang in the Marsyangdi valley. From the top the view takes in Annapurna II, Annapurna IV, Gangapurna, Tilicho Peak and the Manang valley.\nAfter an acclimatisation day at Pisang, you move to base camp and a high camp on a rocky shoulder. The summit day climbs a steep, exposed snow and ice slope on fixed ropes to the top.\nThis is a technical climb at altitude in a short time, so it suits people who are already fit and comfortable with crampons. It can also be added to a full Annapurna Circuit for more gradual acclimatisation."
