    "overview": "Rara is Nepal's largest lake, a sheet of clear blue water at about 2,990 m, ringed by forests of blue pine, spruce and juniper in the far west of the country. It lies within Rara National Park, home to red pandas, musk deer and Himalayan black bears, and visited by migrating waterfowl in winter.\nThis short version flies to the airstrip at Talcha, a few hours' gentle walk from the lake. You have time to walk around the shore and climb to Murma Top for a view over the lake to the distant snow peaks.\nAltitudes are modest and the walking is easy, so the trip suits anyone wanting a peaceful, little-visited corner of Nepal. Flights in the west are weather-dependent, so plans stay flexible.",
